rect response to exactly this issue. So yes, the system isn't perfect. But the benefits IoT provides—energy savings, safety, real-time alerts—are not just theoretical conveniences. They save lives, prevent property damage, and reduce carbon emissions. When weighed against the genuine but manageable problems of e-waste and obsolescence, I still believe the net is positive. And the direction of travel—toward longer support, better recyclability, and secure disposal—gives me confidence that this balance will only improve.
